%description:

Tcp.rtoVarianceFloor:rfc -- the RTO is the estimate, rounded up to the minimum.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "false: RTO = SRTT + 4*RTTVAR, rounded up to minRexmitTimeout (RFC 6298
sections 2.3 and 2.4)".

The classes: rfc (false, the default) and linux (true; LinuxTcp). The code:
TcpAlgorithmBase::rttMeasurementComplete(). This test separates "rfc" from "linux".

Host under test: host1, with the minimum of 1 s, which sends 10000 bytes on a path with a
round trip of 100 ms. Observation: level 2, the signal rto after the first measurement is
max(0.1 + 4 * 0.05, 1) = 1 s.

%# parameter: Tcp.rtoVarianceFloor
%# class: rfc
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.rtoVarianceFloor
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpRtoVarianceFloorRfc")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("rto")
                  .first()
                  .assertValueBetween(0.99, 1.01)
                  .describe("the RTO after the first measurement, the minimum")
                  .within(1.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpRtoVarianceFloorRfc compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.rtoVarianceFloor = false    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 25ms
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpRtoVarianceFloorRfc: PASS
